Code (everything outside data/, rotations/ and docs/) — MIT, see LICENSE.

Data (data/, rotations/, docs/measurements*.md) — CC BY-SA 4.0, see
data/LICENSE. It is derived from the Endfield Talos Wiki
(https://endfield.wiki.gg), licensed CC BY-SA 4.0, and has been modified:
parsed into JSON, with units, roles and effect layouts decided by this
project. Each page's revision id is recorded in data/endfield/raw/ and in
data/endfield/_manifest.json. The effect layers (data/endfield/effects/*.yaml)
quote the wiki's text verbatim in their `seen` fields.

Frame data, skill windows and a few client-side constants are read from a
client datamine (https://github.com/rmxlinux/EndfieldData); only the derived
values are committed, not the dump.

Icons are game assets downloaded from the wiki at build time and are not
committed; they are not covered by the wiki's licence or by this repository's.

The showcase import uses Enka.Network (https://enka.network).
